#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

cat <<'HELP'
Pi workspace quick reference
============================

Start from no tmux sessions:
  pi-start                 Start tmux, ensure pi-personal, and attach to it.
  pi-start secretary       Start/open the secretary grid and attach to it.
  pi-start project [DIR]   Open a project workspace (DIR defaults to $PWD).
  pi-start host            Open pi-personal and select its explicit pi-host pane.
  pi-start all              Start pi-personal and the secretary grid.

Run Pi directly:
  cd REPOSITORY && pi       Normal policy-controlled coding session.
  pi-host                   Explicit unsandboxed host-maintenance session.

Project tmux workspaces:
  cd REPOSITORY && pidev    Neovim on the left, Pi on the right.
  pidev --help              Show the managed project-launcher help.

Tmux sessions and switching:
  Ctrl-a p                  Switch to pi-personal.
  Ctrl-a g                  Switch to pisec (if it is running).
  Ctrl-a \                  Toggle the previous tmux session.
  tmux ls                   List sessions.
  tmux attach -t NAME      Attach to a named session.

Secretary projects:
  pisec                     Open the default registered projects.
  pisec activate ALIAS ... Replace the active project set.
  pisec swap OLD NEW       Replace one active project without changing order.
  pisec list                Print the registered project records.

Recovery:
  pi-start personal         Recreate missing personal panes and attach there.
  pi-personal --ensure     Repair personal panes without switching clients.
  pisec                     Rebuild the secretary grid from the live registry.

The ordinary pi launcher owns workspace selection and sandbox policy. Do not
pass sandbox/trust flags to it; use pi-host only when unsandboxed host access is
intentional.
HELP
